<title>LUXEMBOURG: Ministers formally approve beef labelling rules.</title>
<headline>Ministers formally approve beef labelling rules.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farm ministers formally and unanimously approved a text on compulsory cattle identification and beef labelling rules, EU officials said on Monday.</p>
<p>Portugal and Italy made separate statements to clarify different interpretations over the &quot;competent authority&quot; for implementing the rules.</p>
<p>Last month farm ministers struck a political agreement on a compromise by the Dutch EU Presidency introducing compulsory beef labelling from January 2000 in a bid to restore consumer confidence after the health scare over mad cow disease.</p>
<p>Under the compromise, countries such as Britain and Italy would still be able to make labelling optional for beef sold on their territory.</p>
</text>
